---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaSection from '../../components/CtaSection.astro';
import { graph, breadcrumbs } from '../../lib/schema';
import { EMAIL, BOILERPLATE } from '../../data/site';

const jsonLd = graph(
  breadcrumbs([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Case Studies', path: '/case-studies' },
  ])
);

const stats = [
  { value: '6', label: 'businesses running on our systems' },
  { value: '12+', label: 'automations in production' },
  { value: '67', label: 'real production orders loaded on one system’s day one' },
  { value: '400+', label: 'articles processed every day' },
  { value: '6–8 hrs/day', label: 'of manual operations eliminated for one 6-person team' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Case Studies: Systems and Automations in Production | pocho.tech"
  description="Case studies with real numbers: management systems for a furniture factory, a lube center, and a distributor, plus twelve automations across three teams."
  path="/case-studies"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Six businesses. Real numbers.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Management systems for operations that ran on paper, and AI automations for teams drowning in repetitive work. Every engagement started as a single build; most continue on an embedded retainer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt stats-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The numbers across all of them</h2>
      <div class="stat-strip">
        {stats.map((s) => (
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="stat-value">{s.value}</span>
            <span class="stat-label">{s.label}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="studies">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The case studies</h2>

      <article class="study">
        <h3>67 real orders loaded on day one. 11 were already late.</h3>
        <p class="client-line"><strong>Furniture factory</strong>, sixty workers, made-to-order production.</p>
        <p>We built their production management system and migrated the real operation before switch-on: 67 active orders, 364 pieces, their own order numbers. The first morning, the owner saw the whole backlog on one screen for the first time, and reprioritized the week with data instead of with whoever complained loudest. One feedback round brought 13 change requests; the staged build absorbed them without starting over.</p>
        <a class="study-link" href="/case-studies/furniture-factory">Read the furniture factory case study →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="study">
        <h3>Open on a Monday. Running on its system since the Friday before.</h3>
        <p class="client-line"><strong>Lube center</strong>, a brand-new business opened by the owners of a distributor we work with.</p>
        <p>Instead of opening on paper and migrating later, the business was born digital: service orders, multi-service checklists, scheduling, and invoicing, live before the first customer walked in. It runs on the counter phone and the office computer alike. There was never a double-entry period.</p>
        <a class="study-link" href="/case-studies/lube-center">Read the lube center case study →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="study">
        <h3>2–4 proposals a day, 15 minutes each.</h3>
        <p class="client-line"><strong>Event production agency</strong>, team of six to eight.</p>
        <p>An accepted proposal in Fresh Proposals updates the HubSpot deal stage, builds the Monday.com board, and creates the QuickBooks customer with two invoices split 50/50, untouched. Four automations run their back office; this pipeline alone removes 6–8 hours of manual operations from every working day.</p>
        <p class="no-testimonial">No testimonial on file. The events agency refers new business instead.</p>
        <a class="study-link" href="/case-studies/event-production-agency">Read the event production agency case study →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="study">
        <h3>From zero operational visibility to automated daily reporting.</h3>
        <p class="client-line"><strong>EdTech workforce training</strong>, Boston. 30–40 applicants per cohort, 12–16 accepted.</p>
        <p>Six connected systems run admissions and operations: AI-scored interviews from Read.ai transcripts, automated scheduling, stipend-eligibility alerts, real-time dashboards, and the 5pm report the whole team reads.</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>"You have done such a great job that I can't remember how we were working before you."</p>
          <cite>CEO, EdTech workforce-training company</cite>
        </blockquote>
        <a class="study-link" href="/case-studies/edtech-workforce-training">Read the EdTech workforce training case study →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="study">
        <h3>400+ articles a day. Ten make the newsletter.</h3>
        <p class="client-line"><strong>Travel media company</strong>, editorial team of twelve.</p>
        <p>Overnight, an AI reads eleven-plus publications, picks the ten stories that matter, and delivers a finished newsletter every morning. The creator tracker went from 5 hours a week to 1.5, covering 70 creators instead of 30.</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>"Erick has helped us build and implement multiple automations for our editorial department, and these save us time each week that can be spent producing content rather than sifting through emails and data."</p>
          <cite>Editorial team, travel media company</cite>
        </blockquote>
        <a class="study-link" href="/case-studies/travel-media-company">Read the travel media company case study →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection
    heading="Tell me where the hours go."
    body="Sixty minutes: you walk me through how your team works, and I tell you what I'd automate first and what it would cost."
    secondaryLabel={EMAIL}
    secondaryHref={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="boilerplate">{BOILERPLATE}</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: var(--space-section) clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px); }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .stats-section { padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px); }
  .stat-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
    gap: 36px 32px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .stat-value {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--c-red);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .stat-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
    max-width: 26ch;
  }

  .studies { padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px) 0; }
  .study {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    padding-block: clamp(44px, 6vw, 72px);
  }
  .study:first-of-type { margin-top: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .study h3 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .client-line { color: var(--c-text-mute); }
  .client-line strong { color: var(--c-text); }
  .no-testimonial { color: var(--c-text-dim); font-size: 0.95rem; }

  blockquote {
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 26px 30px;
    margin: 24px 0;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  blockquote p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--c-text);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  blockquote cite {
    display: block;
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--c-text-mute);
  }

  .study-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .boilerplate {
    color: var(--c-text-dim);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 40px 0 0;
    max-width: 75ch;
  }
</style>
